<p>Mark Murphy, currently professor and chair of <a href="https://philosophy.georgetown.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">philosophy at Georgetown University</a>, will be moving to the <a href="https://philosophy.nd.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Notre Dame</a>. <span id="more-57264"></span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-57267 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/murphy-mark.jpg" alt="" width="225" height="225" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/murphy-mark.jpg 225w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/murphy-mark-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/murphy-mark-177x177.jpg 177w" sizes="(max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px" /></p>
<p><a href="https://gufaculty360.georgetown.edu/s/contact/00336000014RcE9AAK/mark-c-murphy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Professor Murphy</a> is known for his work in moral philosophy, philosophy of law, and philosophy of religion. He is the author of <i>God&#8217;s Own Ethics: Norms of Divine Action and the Argument from Evil</i> (OUP, 2017) and <em>God and Moral Law: On the Theistic Explanation of Morality</em> (OUP, 2011), among many other works. You can learn more about his books and articles <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/mark-c-murphy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>He will be taking up his new position as Cathy and Jack Brennan Professor of Virtue Ethics at Notre Dame (where he earned his MA and PhD), in the fall.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/05/29/murphy-from-georgetown-to-notre-dame/">Murphy from Georgetown to Notre Dame</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>